From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] loader: end a child whose private ntdll copy failed

A child fell back to the shared ntdll when its own copy failed, and the
shared copy's .data cannot start a second process, so it crashed later.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-24-bootstrap.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/loader_ios.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/loader_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/loader_ios.c
index 1c296de..43a775c 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/loader_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/loader_ios.c
@@ -3320,7 +3320,17 @@ DECLSPEC_EXPORT void wine_ios_child_main( int argc, char *argv[], int child_fd_s
 
             if (ios_jit_copy_module_for_child(pLdrInitializeThunk, child_peb) != 0)
             {
-                dprintf(STDERR_FILENO, "[Wine child] ntdll copy FAILED — falling back to SHARED ntdll (module lists will collide!)\n");
+                /* Playport: the shared ntdll cannot start a child. Its .data
+                 * is the parent's, so loader_init finds the imports already
+                 * fixed up, takes the thread-attach branch, and thread_attach
+                 * reads the child PEB's NULL LdrData (fault at 0x30, then a
+                 * crash cascade in the fault handlers). The copy fails when the
+                 * JIT pool is exhausted, so end the child with STATUS_NO_MEMORY,
+                 * as a failed image map does: NtTerminateProcess records the
+                 * exit code and abort_process() ends only this pseudo-process. */
+                dprintf(STDERR_FILENO, "[Wine child] ntdll copy FAILED — ending the child with STATUS_NO_MEMORY\n");
+                NtTerminateProcess( GetCurrentProcess(), STATUS_NO_MEMORY );
+                return;
             }
             else
             {
